From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Baker <dylan.c.baker@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 21:44:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nir: Add an unreachable default to generated switch statement

Coverity notices that there's no requirement that the bit_size must be 64, 32,
or 16. While currently this unreachable cannot be reached, it seems better to
have something here to catch a theoritcal float8 or float128 than to let it
silently fall through.

Fixes: 32e91a74675 ("nir: add new float multiply-add opcodes")
CID: 1696245
Reviewed-by: Karol Herbst <kherbst@redhat.com>
Reviewed-by: Eric Engestrom <eric@engestrom.ch>
(cherry picked from commit db1325d214f4f045ab37f119398cbccdd32a8eeb)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/43884>
(cherry picked from commit 7bd6535e1c1103c178529ef5eaed65446cf62a17)
---
 src/compiler/nir/nir_constant_expressions.py | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/compiler/nir/nir_constant_expressions.py b/src/compiler/nir/nir_constant_expressions.py
index dcc9e2677c2..be595c7fbad 100644
--- a/src/compiler/nir/nir_constant_expressions.py
+++ b/src/compiler/nir/nir_constant_expressions.py
@@ -122,6 +122,9 @@ handle_intermediate_float_result(double value, unsigned execution_mode, unsigned
         } else {
             const_val.u16 = _mesa_float_to_float16_rtne(value);
         }
+        break;
+    default:
+        UNREACHABLE("Unsupported bit_size. Should be 64, 32, or 16");
     }
 
     return get_float_source(const_val, execution_mode, bit_size);
-- 
